The evidence is consistent, so here is the write-up.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "ts-payment-service",
      "fault_kind": "pod_failure",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT metric, attr_k8s_pod_name, min(value) mn, max(value) mx FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric='k8s.container.restarts' AND attr_k8s_pod_name LIKE 'ts-payment-service%' GROUP BY 1,2",
          "claim": "ts-payment-service-5ff6f7b6ff-vpt9v container restarts rise from 0 to 1 in the abnormal window (0 in normal)."
        },
        {
          "kind": "log",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, level, message FROM abnormal_logs WHERE service_name='ts-payment-service' AND message LIKE '%initialization completed%' LIMIT 5",
          "claim": "Payment logs a full Spring startup ('initialization completed in 7897 ms') during the incident, showing the instance restarted."
        },
        {
          "kind": "log",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, level, left(message,200) msg FROM abnormal_logs WHERE service_name='ts-inside-payment-service' AND level='SEVERE' LIMIT 5",
          "claim": "Inside-payment logs 503 'upstream connect error' exceptions when calling payment, consistent with payment being down."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "ts-payment-service",
      "to": "ts-inside-payment-service",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT c.service_name caller, c.attr_http_response_status_code code, round(c.duration/1e6,1) call_ms, s.service_name callee FROM abnormal_traces c LEFT JOIN abnormal_traces s ON s.trace_id=c.trace_id AND s.parent_span_id=c.span_id WHERE c.service_name='ts-inside-payment-service' AND c.span_name='POST' ORDER BY c.duration DESC LIMIT 25",
          "claim": "Inside-payment's POSTs to payment fail with 503 after about 3.5 s and have no payment server span; successful calls take about 20 ms."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "from": "ts-inside-payment-service",
      "to": "ts-ui-dashboard",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_http_response_status_code code, attr_status_code st, count(*) n, round(approx_quantile(duration/1e6,0.5),1) p50_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE span_name LIKE '%inside_pay%' GROUP BY 1,2,3,4 ORDER BY 1,3",
          "claim": "Inside-payment's inside_payment endpoint returns 500 errors at about 3.5 s p50; user-facing dashboard requests to it slow to 20 s timeouts."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```
